Package: cmdlaplacer
Title: Build 'Laplace' Models and Run Them with 'cmdstanr'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Metodi", "Latinov", , "latinovmetodi@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: A thin R wrapper around the 'Laplace' compiler, which turns
    '.laplace' source files (Stan plus a package manager and namespaced
    imports) into plain, inspectable '.stan' files. Builds a model and hands
    it to 'cmdstanr', adds git-hosted 'Laplace' libraries to a project, and
    can install the 'laplace' command-line tool itself.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/mlatinov/cmdlaplacer, https://github.com/mlatinov/laplace
BugReports: https://github.com/mlatinov/cmdlaplacer/issues
Imports:
    utils
Suggests:
    cmdstanr
Additional_repositories: https://stan-dev.r-universe.dev
SystemRequirements: laplace (https://github.com/mlatinov/laplace); git and
    cargo to install it with laplace_install()
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 8.0.0
